# ThreadSanitizer suppressions. Qt from the distro is not TSan-instrumented, so synchronisation that
# happens entirely inside Qt (QThreadPool, QWaitCondition, QMutex fast paths) is invisible to TSan
# and reported as races. Only Qt-internal frames are suppressed; races involving our code still fail.
called_from_lib:libQt6Core.so.6
# The QML engine allocates on the GUI thread and frees on its type-loader thread, synchronised inside Qt Qml.
called_from_lib:libQt6Qml.so.6
# Qt Quick's pixmap reader thread receives its jobs (URL, requested size) from the GUI thread through Qt's own
# locking; an image provider reading them on that thread is reported. Its frames carry no symbols, so the module
# is matched: reports with a Qt Quick frame on either side are hidden, races between our own threads still fail.
race:libQt6Quick.so.6
race:QWaitCondition
race:QThreadPoolPrivate
race:QThreadPoolThread
mutex:QWaitCondition
# QThread finishes and is waited for, but Qt detaches/joins it inside the uninstrumented library.
thread:QThread::start
# Qt's event dispatcher on Linux is GLib's main loop; its wakeup fd is signalled and closed under GLib's own
# (uninstrumented) locking.
race:g_wakeup_signal
race:g_wakeup_free
# A receiver's ~QObject calls sender->metaObject() (for disconnectNotify) while holding the receiver's
# signalSlotLock; a sender being destroyed on another thread blocks on that lock before it is freed (see the
# comment in Qt's ~QObject). With the lock inside uninstrumented Qt, the read of a CallbackChannel's vptr there is
# reported against its delete on the owner thread (image://cover shutdown test).
race:noctara::net::CallbackChannel::metaObject
# libdbus (QtDBus' connection thread) is uninstrumented: TSan sees only its pthread mutexes, so a mutex block it
# frees and reallocates, or its own lock ordering, is reported against the GUI thread's dbus_connection_* calls.
called_from_lib:libdbus-1.so.3
# QtDBus is uninstrumented as well: messages built on its connection thread are freed on the GUI thread (pending call
# replies), and libdbus' mutex is taken inside libdbus (ignored above) while dbus_message_unref is tail-called from
# QtDBus, so TSan sees the matching unlock come from libQt6DBus. Reports with a QtDBus frame are hidden.
race:libQt6DBus.so.6
mutex:libQt6DBus.so.6
# The raster paint engine splits large fills across Qt's own thread pool (qdrawhelper.cpp); the runnable's hand-off
# happens inside uninstrumented Qt, so its delete on the pool thread is reported against its new on the GUI thread.
race:qdrawhelper.cpp
